  "title": "Coast Guard delivers pumps, saves boat and crew",
  "description": "A U.S. Coast Guard aircrew aboard an MH-60 Jayhawk helicopter assigned to Sector Columbia River, delivers dewatering pumps to a vessel taking on water 66 miles west of Tillamook Head on the Oregon Coast, Aug. 8, 2017. The Coast Guard delivered three pumps to the commercial fishing vessel Pura Vida to dewater the vessel, and a crew aboard a 47-foot Motor Life Boat assigned to Station Cape Disappointment towed the Pura Vida to shore. (U.S Coast Guard video)",
